 "final_result": "Completed the full three-script SrTiO3 DFT band-structure workflow.\n\n**Materials Project ID:** mp-5229 (SrTiO3, Pm-3m #221)\n\n**Atom count:** 5 atoms before and after primitive-cell reduction (the MP cell is already primitive for this perovskite).\n\n**Workflow outline:**\n1. Fetched base SrTiO3 CIF from Materials Project (mp-5229, Pm-3m #221), reduced to primitive cell via chem_llm.kpath (5 atoms, unchanged).\n2. generate_structures.py: wrote 51 structures (000 unperturbed + 50 perturbed with thermal displacements at T=300 K and random strain <0.5%). Per-species RMS displacements: O=0.122 A, Ti=0.089 A, Sr=0.063 A.\n3. Fetched pseudopotentials (nc, pbesol, stringent, UPF, scalar-relativistic) for Sr (z_val=10), Ti (z_val=12), O (z_val=6). Total electrons = 40, occupied bands = 20.\n4. setup_jobs.py: created calculations/NNN/ for all 51 structures with pw.in (SCF), bands.in (NSCF), bands_post.in (bands.x). ecutwfc=92 Ry (46 Ha \u00d7 2), ecutrho=368 Ry, occupations='fixed', conv_thr=1e-8, nspin=1, nbnd=40, SCF k-mesh 7\u00d77\u00d77, bands k-points from kpath.\n5. Ran run_espresso_workflow on calculations/000: success (scf=11.5s, bands_scf=33.2s, bands_post=5.1s).\n6. plot_bands.py: plotted band structure aligned to VBM, saved to calculations/000/bands_000.pdf.\n\n**ASE functions used:** ase.io.read/write (CIF I/O), ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in (QE input files), ase.Atoms (structure representation).\n\n**Band gap obtained:** 1.84 eV (PBEsol, scalar-relativistic). VBM=9.832 eV, CBM=11.672 eV (absolute energies from QE).\n\n**Scientific assumptions:**\n- T=300 K for thermal displacements: cubic SrTiO3 is stable above Tc~105 K (ferroelectric transition), so 300 K is appropriate.\n- Scalar-relativistic pseudopotentials: all elements have Z<54 (Sr=38, Ti=22, O=8), no spin-orbit physics targeted.\n- occupations='fixed': SrTiO3 is a semiconductor (gap ~1.77 eV from MP), not a metal.\n- nspin=1: no magnetism (moment=0 from MP).\n- ecutwfc=92 Ry: max recommended cutoff 46 Ha (O) \u00d7 2 Ry/Ha (INVARIANT 5).\n- nbnd=40: 2\u00d7 occupied bands (20), padded for conduction bands.\n\n**Items for expert review:**\n- The band gap of 1.84 eV is slightly larger than the experimental ~1.77 eV, which is typical for PBEsol (known to underestimate gaps, but here it's close).\n- The thermal displacement amplitudes are approximate (based on typical neutron diffraction U values at 300 K) and could be refined with a phonon calculation.\n- The SCF k-mesh (7\u00d77\u00d77) was chosen by scf_kmesh for a non-metal; convergence testing would be needed for production-quality results.",
